e {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438994}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47b66471-b70f-5509-8368-6a6674b74447" :question/math-academy-id "q-141078" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)={e}^{2x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)={e}^{2x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{2x})}^{′} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y={e}^{2x}$ and ${y}^{′}=2{e}^{2x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}2y \\\\ 2{e}^{2x} & =2{e}^{2x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272196 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58cf84e4-bf37-53ee-9c4e-c48312865eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437932} {:answer/id #uuid "7c777b71-5609-57b6-98cd-5de6ad97f13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58cf84e4-bf37-53ee-9c4e-c48312865eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186