eld.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439015}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8806c061-892c-5fd2-baf1-cd903aa5ea31" :question/math-academy-id "q-141089" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{2y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-3{x}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-5x$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-3{x}^{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-3{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-6x \\\\  & \\ne -5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=-3{x}^{2}$ and ${y}^{′}=-6x$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ -6x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2(-3{x}^{2})}{x} \\\\ -6x & =-6x\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-3{x}^{2}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0077f4e-bfef-5c44-9c4f-22e790c66054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494118} {:answer/id #uuid "f470c94f-5751-5b47-a030-8985df3f2d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f470c94f-5751-5b47-a030-8985df3f2d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494120} :answer-field/id #uuid "276d5850-899a-5418-b118-58774ff396c5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494089} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0427735-f1b6-5953-9a58-65ffe3fc0cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494104} {:answer/id #uuid "d93ba829-e163-58c2-b76e-e291c5f8be1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d93ba829-e163-58c2-b76e-e291c5f8be1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494113} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc47d48-c82a-5502-bb58-b7f089ff6b6b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494102} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c3effa8-82fb-5fb4-8d49-078df0fff8cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494098} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb4386c-3ca1-56b1-a1f1-27eda3db5ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbb4386c-3ca1-56b1-a1f1-27eda3db5ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494122} :answer-field/id #uuid "b26b8e2c-d5f7-5d56-ac89-1e186c2dea2a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494107}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03ad73f2-dfe8-5b7e-bde4-05067dff734f" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{3y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{′}(x)=-5{x}^{2}$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-2{x}^{3},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-2{x}^{3})}^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-6{x}^{2} \\\\  & \\ne -5{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=-2{x}^{3}$ and ${y}^{′}=-6{x}^{2}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3y}{x} \\\\ -6{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3(-2{x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ -6{x}^{2} & =-6{x}^{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=-2{x}^{3}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4330cfb7-8007-5f4b-b65a-6b8ca9b8b25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494094} {:answer/id #uuid "8a470ecb-d8a1-5134-bd03-7aa6af28cd48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a470ecb-d8a1-5134-bd03-7aa6af28cd48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494101} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fa5a541-2f14-5a90-830a-7537bc62c9fb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494083} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b03c25e-572f-53bd-97e2-15a9854478d8" :answer/type {:db/iden